---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
const pageTitle = 'Evaluation Framework & Editorial Methodology — The HR Stack Guide';
const pageHeading = 'Evaluation Framework & Editorial Methodology';
const pageDescription =
  'At The HR Stack Guide, we evaluate B2B HR software using a standardized 4-pillar framework. Every rating, data matrix, and comparison pair across Global Payroll & EOR, Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS), and Performance Management is scored against this rubric.';
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  heading={pageHeading}
  description={pageDescription}
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-14">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
          <li><a href="/" class="transition hover:text-indigo-600">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true" class="text-slate-300">&gt;</li>
          <li class="font-medium text-indigo-600" aria-current="page">Methodology</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        {pageHeading}
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
      <section>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          At The HR Stack Guide, we evaluate B2B HR software using a standardized 4-pillar framework. Every
          rating, data matrix, and comparison pair across Global Payroll &amp; EOR, Applicant Tracking Systems
          (ATS), and Performance Management is scored against this rubric.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 1: Transparent Pricing &amp; True Cost of Ownership (TCO)</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          We look beyond advertised starting prices to calculate actual operating costs. Our analysis breaks
          down base platform fees, per-employee-per-month (PEPM) rates, implementation fees, currency
          conversion markups, deposit requirements, and contract cancellation terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 2: Feature Depth, Security &amp; Compliance</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          We evaluate whether platforms meet regulatory and enterprise operational standards:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>
            <strong>Payroll &amp; EOR:</strong> Owned-entity networks vs. third-party reliance, automated
            localized tax withholding, statutory benefits, and IP assignment protections.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>ATS:</strong> GDPR/CCPA compliance, EEOC/OFCCP tracking, structured interviewing rubrics,
            and automated candidate consent workflows.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Performance Management:</strong> Role-based access controls (RBAC), SOC 2 Type II
            certifications, 360-degree review privacy, and audit logging.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 3: Integration Ecosystem &amp; Usability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          We test how well each platform fits into an existing tech stack. This includes evaluating native
          integrations with accounting software (QuickBooks, NetSuite, Xero), communication tools (Slack,
          Teams), identity providers (Okta, Google Workspace), and REST API accessibility for custom
          workflows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 4: Data Verification &amp; Editorial Independence</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Our data matrices are compiled using primary vendor documentation, verified API specs, public
          changelogs, and hands-on trial environment testing.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>
            <strong>No Paid Placement:</strong> Vendors cannot pay for higher rankings, preferred badge
            placements, or altered performance scores.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Affiliate Separation:</strong> Commercial affiliate relationships are handled separately
            from our scoring methodology.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Fact-Checking:</strong> We re-audit comparison data on a scheduled basis and update our
            published dates whenever material features or prices change.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Questions &amp; Methodological Corrections</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          If you have questions about our testing criteria or need to report a data discrepancy, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:dave@thehrstackguide.com" class="font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:underline">dave@thehrstackguide.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
